 Pulse is an internal market-insights dashboard. It shows key figures, a sortable table of instruments, a watchlist, top movers and recent activity; the house portfolio with an allocation chart; a filterable, paginated trade blotter with a detail drawer; an instrument page with price history, key stats and recent trades; a searchable client list with a detail drawer and client notes; a list of daily reports with status badges; notifications in the top bar; and user settings (theme and notifications) saved in the browser.
 
-Routes: `/` dashboard, `/portfolio`, `/trades`, `/instruments/:symbol`, `/clients`, `/reports`, `/settings`.
+Routes: `/sign-in`, `/` dashboard, `/portfolio`, `/trades`, `/venues`, `/instruments/:symbol`, `/clients`, `/reports`, `/settings`. Every route except `/sign-in` needs a signed-in user.
+
+## Sign-in
+
+Pulse asks for an email and a password at `/sign-in`. The mock accounts are in `src/data/users.json`: `dana@pulse.test` and `owen@pulse.test` (admins), `marc@pulse.test` (trader) and `ines@pulse.test` (analyst).
+
+- There is no shared or demo password and no passwordless "claim" page; one password only works for its own account.
+- Every sign-in failure shows the same message, "Wrong email or password.", and nothing ever locks an account.
+- The session is the user's email, saved as a JSON string under `pulse.session`. A reload keeps you signed in, and "Sign out" in the user menu removes it. People who already have that key stay signed in.
+- Every user except the admins must choose a new password the first time they sign in (at least 10 characters, typed twice). Chosen passwords are kept in this browser under `pulse.passwords`; after that the old password stops working and nobody is asked again.
+
+## Settings and navigation
+
+Preferences are saved under `pulse.settings` as `{ "theme", "alerts": { "email", "digest" }, "navbar" }`. A value in the old flat shape (`emailAlerts`, `pushAlerts`, `weeklyDigest`) is converted when Pulse loads and written back; push alerts were never used and are gone. The conversion lives in `src/utils/settings.ts`.
+
+The navigation has three variants, chosen in Settings under Appearance as "Navigation style": `sidebar` (the default), `compact` (a narrow sidebar with the first letter of each page and the full name as tooltip) and `top` (the links in the top bar). The variant name is on the `Primary` navigation as `data-variant`. The links and the top bar titles come from one list in `src/components/pages.ts`.
+
+The Venues page (`/venues`) counts the trades, and how many ended filled, partially filled and cancelled, for each venue. It is laid out like the Trades page.
 
 All data is mocked: typed fetchers in `src/api` read JSON files in `src/data` after a short artificial delay.
 
